# Add a route to a Rivet app

1. Pick the file under `src/routes/` (URL = path): `about.tsx` → `/about`, `blog/[slug].tsx` → `/blog/:slug`, `docs/[[lang]]/x.tsx` (optional param), `files/[...path].tsx` (rest), `(group)/p.tsx` → `/p` (shares the group's `_layout.tsx`), `api/time.ts` → endpoint (`export const GET = onGet(() => Response.json(…))`, `onGet` from `@rivetjs/router`). `_layout.tsx` wraps its folder; `_404.tsx` / `_error.tsx` handle misses / errors. Look up details with `get_doc("docs:/guides/routing/file-routes/")`.
2. Write the page. Server code lives in exports wrapped in a `@rivetjs/router` call — `load(…)`, `actions(…)`, `guard(…)`, `onGet(…)` … (stripped from the browser build):

```tsx
import { notFound, type PageProps, type RequestEvent, load } from "@rivetjs/router";

export const loader = load(async ({ params }: RequestEvent<"blog/[slug]">) => {
  const post = await findPost(params.slug); // server-only: database, files, secrets
  if (!post) throw notFound();
  return { post };
});

export const head = { title: "Post" };

export default function Post({ data }: PageProps<"blog/[slug]">) {
  return <h1 class="text-2xl">{data.post.title}</h1>;
}
```

- Page props `data`, `params`, `url` are plain values; in `_layout.tsx` (`LayoutProps`) they are accessors: `data()`, `params()`, `url()`, plus `children`.
- Mutations: `export const forms = actions({ name: async ({ request }) => … })` + `<form method="post" action="?/name">`; with validation use `@rivetjs/forms` (`action(def, fn)` from `@rivetjs/forms/server`).
- Access checks: `guard(…)` (throw / return `redirect()`, `deny()`, `notFound()`).
- Static mode (`rivetRouter({ mode: "static" })`): `load(…)` runs at build time; dynamic `[param]` pages list their params in `entries(…)`.
- Server-only helpers go in `*.server.ts` files (browser code cannot import them: RV3008).

3. Link to it: plain `<a href="/blog/hello">` (client navigation), or typed `<Link to="/blog/hello">` from `@rivetjs/router/link`; programmatic `navigate()` from `@rivetjs/router/client`.
4. Run `npm run check` (`rivet sync` regenerates the typed routes in `.rivet/`, `rivet-check` reports `RV` codes; RV3101 = a link matches no route). Fix every diagnostic (`explain_diagnostic(code)`), then `npm run build`.
